# Line-ending policy for this repo.
# Store text normalized as LF in git; check out with the platform's native EOL
# (CRLF on Windows, LF on macOS/Linux). This is independent of each developer's
# core.autocrlf setting, so checkouts are deterministic.
* text=auto

# Exception: the minijinja segmenter golden gate (tests/minijinja.segment-golden.test.ts) locks
# segment()'s exact output byte-for-byte, and segment()'s own contract is to PRESERVE whatever
# newline convention its input uses — so the platform's native-EOL checkout above makes these
# fixtures (and the golden values recorded from them) genuinely different strings on Windows vs
# Linux/macOS, and the golden comparison fails on whichever platform didn't generate it. Pinned to
# LF unconditionally so the checked-out bytes — and therefore segment()'s output — are identical on
# every platform. Not a workaround: this is what a byte-exact golden test requires from its input.
tests/fixtures/minijinja/*.sql text eol=lf
tests/golden/minijinja-segment.golden.json text eol=lf
